WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.552
A new certificate

00:00:01.364 --> 00:00:02.413
format built for

00:00:02.225 --> 00:00:03.404
post-quantum web

00:00:03.942 --> 00:00:05.439
An IETF draft

00:00:05.251 --> 00:00:06.159
from authors at

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:06.595
Google

00:00:06.713 --> 00:00:07.338
Apple

00:00:07.397 --> 00:00:09.048
Cloudflare and Geomys

00:00:08.977 --> 00:00:10.250
defines Merkle Tree

00:00:10.062 --> 00:00:11.135
certificates a

00:00:11.206 --> 00:00:12.055
new kind of

00:00:11.937 --> 00:00:12.656
X .

00:00:12.468 --> 00:00:14.036
509 certificate

00:00:14.175 --> 00:00:15.059
It comes from

00:00:14.871 --> 00:00:16.168
the IETF's PLANTS

00:00:15.979 --> 00:00:16.804
working group

00:00:17.326 --> 00:00:18.611
They build Certificate

00:00:18.423 --> 00:00:19.849
Transparency style

00:00:19.661 --> 00:00:20.851
public logging into

00:00:20.663 --> 00:00:22.090
the certificate itself

00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:23.552
cutting overhead as

00:00:23.364 --> 00:00:24.979
certificates get shorter

00:00:24.791 --> 00:00:26.323
lived and post-quantum

00:00:26.135 --> 00:00:27.432
signatures get much

00:00:27.243 --> 00:00:27.974
larger

00:00:28.502 --> 00:00:29.622
An optional mode

00:00:29.434 --> 00:00:31.343
skips signatures entirely

00:00:31.155 --> 00:00:32.322
for relying parties

00:00:32.134 --> 00:00:32.924
that stay up

00:00:32.736 --> 00:00:33.348
to date

00:00:33.487 --> 00:00:34.419
This is draft

00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:35.220
number 8 from

00:00:35.032 --> 00:00:36.742
November 2026

00:00:37.278 --> 00:00:38.292
Full story on

00:00:38.103 --> 00:00:38.999
the dashboard
